  "id": "EDU018",
  "title": "The Bent Straw Detective",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "everyday science",
  "premise": "An illustrator wants to draw a straw crossing a water surface, but a straight copied line misses its apparent bend. A ray overlay distinguishes the physical straw from the changing path of light.",
  "hook": "Did the straw bend, or did the light change direction?",
  "visible_action": "A rigid straw stays still while selected light rays bend at the water boundary and an apparent image shifts.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Refraction can change the apparent position of a submerged object.",
  "gate": "Review refractive geometry and observer position; mark apparent and physical locations separately.",
